To add a link to every post, you can modify your existing Nginx configuration by adding a block of code that generates a link for each post. Here's an updated example:
```nginx
# index.html fallback
location / {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index index.html index.htm;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;

    # Add a block to generate links for each post
    if (-d $document_root/posts) {
        set $posts "";
        set $counter 0;
        /usr/bin/ls -1 $document_root/posts/*.md > /tmp/posts_list;
        while read post.file; do
            set $posts "$posts<a href=\"/post/$post.file\">$post.file</a> ";
            set $counter $counter + 1;
        done < /tmp/posts_list;
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    }
}

# Serve individual posts
location ~ ^/post/(.*)\.md {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html/posts;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /post/$1.html;
}
```
This code uses the `ls` command to list all the `.md` files in the `/posts` directory, and then loops through the list to generate a link for each post. The links are then added to the HTML index page.

